ages in cardiovascular medicine. Late enhancement of a left ventricular cardiac fibroma assessed with gadolinium-enhanced cardiovascular magnetic resonance</article-title><source>Circulation</source><year>2005</year><volume>112</volume><fpage>E242</fpage><lpage>E243</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16186429</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B12"><label>12</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Webb</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name><name><surname>Osborne</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cardiac rhabdomyomas and their association with tuberous sclerosis</article-title><source>Arch Dis Child</source><year>1993</year><volume>68</volume><fpage>367</fpage><lpage>370</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8466239</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B13"><label>13</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Newell</surname><given-names>JD</given-names><suffix>2nd</suffix></name><name><surname>Eckel</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Davis</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Tadros</surname><given-names>NB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>MR appearance of an arteriovenous hemangioma of the interventricular septum</article-title><source>Cardiovasc Intervent Radiol</source><year>1988</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>319</fpage><lpage>321</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3145803</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B14"><label>14</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yahata</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Endo</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Honma</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Ino</surname><given-name